diff --git a/docs/build/HIP.md b/docs/build/HIP.md
index 5d423d48..521b6c88 100644
--- a/docs/build/HIP.md
+++ b/docs/build/HIP.md
@@ -424,3 +424,24 @@ These are skipped entirely on HIP builds. To enable GPU acceleration for ISTFT a
 - GGML HIP backend CMake: `external/ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt`
 - GGML backend registry: `external/ggml/src/ggml-backend-reg.cpp` (L116: HIP registers via `GGML_USE_CUDA`)
 - llama.cpp HIP build docs: `docs/build.md` (upstream GGML documentation)
+
+## Optional Halo implementation
+
+Use `--backend hip --backend-impl halo` to select the opt-in Strix Halo
+(gfx1151) kernel implementation. Omit `--backend-impl` to retain existing HIP
+execution. The server accepts the same flag, or `"backend_impl": "halo"` next
+to `"backend": "hip"` in its configuration.
+
+Halo specializes eligible large F32 matrix multiplications and 1D convolution
+patch extraction (`im2col`). Other operations use existing HIP kernels. Eligible
+default-precision matrix multiplications may round operands to BF16 and accumulate
+in F32; explicit F32 computation and explicit operation lowerings take precedence.
+Weights on disk are unchanged. Audio can differ numerically from default HIP.
+Unsupported implementation/device combinations fail initialization.
+
+Selection belongs to each backend instance and is independent of model
+`perf_mode` presets. The C++ API uses `BackendConfig::implementation`; the C API
+provides `audiocpp_session_create_with_implementation` without changing the
+existing backend-config structure. GGML exposes implementation discovery,
+initialization and identity through optional backend registry hooks, so other
+backends need no changes until they provide an alternative implementation.
